{"name":"Medlar","hex":"#d5d7bf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"medlar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Mespilus germanica, common medlar (now often Crataegus germanica).","Any tree of the genus Mespilus, now Crataegus sect. Mespilus, including many species now in other genera."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medlar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Medlar (musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Medlar is the stage name of the British deep house producer Ned Pegler. His first releases were published in 2010 under his alias Klic on his co-owned label Hit and Hope. Since 2011 he releases under the London-based Wolf Music label."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medlar_(musician)","wikidata":"Q20795025"},{"title":"Mespilus germanica","blocks":[{"text":"Mespilus germanica, known as the medlar or common medlar, is a large shrub or small tree in the rose family Rosaceae. When the genus Mespilus is included in the genus Crataegus, the correct name for this species is Crataegus germanica (L.) Kuntze."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Medlar_pomes_and_leaves.jpg/330px-Medlar_pomes_and_leaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mespilus_germanica","wikidata":"Q146186"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Mespilus_germanica_imbrication.jpg/500px-Mespilus_germanica_imbrication.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Mespilus_germanica_imbrication.jpg/500px-Mespilus_germanica_imbrication.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMespilus_germanica_imbrication.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/20150511Crataegus_germanica5.jpg/500px-20150511Crataegus_germanica5.